You can use the `openapi_extra` parameter to document a custom request body schema when bypassing FastAPI's integrated Pydantic validation and JSON parsing, such as in the case of YAML content.

For example:

```python
@app.post(
    "/items/",
    openapi_extra={
        "requestBody": {
            "content": {
                "application/yaml": {
                    "schema": {
                        "type": "object",
                        "properties": {
                            "name": {"type": "string"},
                            "price": {"type": "integer"}
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
)
```

This will define a custom OpenAPI schema for the request body, even if you're not using FastAPI's integrated validation and JSON parsing.
